// The heralds of the game's towns, adopted: the first of the emulator's conversations this game plays.
//
// Each of these people tells a player about places on their world and puts a waypoint on the one asked
// about. The conversation is the emulator's structure in the client's own words (`core3ref/
// conversations.json`); all its handler did besides follow the links was to put that waypoint down when a
// screen named `loc1` to `loc4` (and `loc1a`, the first said another way) was reached, at the place the
// emulator's herald table gives that number. So each tree here takes its waypoints from that table
// (`"waypoints": "heralds"`, `core3Trees.ts`), quest-coloured, named in the client's own words, and the
// handler has nothing left to do.
//
// Seven of the eight: Tatooine's second herald charges for some places and adds the answers that pay
// from its own code, which is left unadopted until that is written fresh here.
{
  "format": 1,
  "credit": "Conversation structure from SWGEmu Core3's scripts (MMOCoreORB/bin/scripts, AGPL-3.0, https://github.com/swgemu/Core3): screen names and links only; the words are the client's own.",
  "trees": {
    "heraldCorellia1ConvoTemplate": { "waypoints": "heralds" },
    "heraldCorellia2ConvoTemplate": { "waypoints": "heralds" },
    "heraldLok1ConvoTemplate": { "waypoints": "heralds" },
    "heraldLok2ConvoTemplate": { "waypoints": "heralds" },
    "heraldNaboo1ConvoTemplate": { "waypoints": "heralds" },
    "heraldNaboo2ConvoTemplate": { "waypoints": "heralds" },
    "heraldTatooine1ConvoTemplate": { "waypoints": "heralds" }
  }
}
